<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mona Passage</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mona Passage is the strait between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> Sea. About 130 km wide and broken by the islands of Mona, Monito and Desecheo, it was crossed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> canoes long before Spanish contact, connecting the chiefdom of Higüey in eastern Hispaniola with Puerto Rico, and later became an important shipping route.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mona-passage.jpg" alt="Mona Passage" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USGS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mona_passage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
